# Vercel Web Analytics Implementation

## Summary
Successfully implemented Vercel Web Analytics for this static HTML greeting card project.

## Changes Made

### Modified Files:
- **greeting-card/index.html** - Added Vercel Web Analytics script tags

## Implementation Details

Since this is a **static HTML project** (not a framework-based application), I followed the official Vercel documentation for HTML/static sites implementation.

### What was added:
1. **Analytics initialization script** - Added `window.va` function to queue analytics calls before the script loads
2. **CDN script tag** - Added the deferred Vercel Analytics script from `https://cdn.vercel-insights.com/v1/script.js`

The implementation was added to the `<head>` section of the HTML file, immediately after the `<title>` tag, following best practices for loading analytics scripts.

## Documentation Reference
- Fetched latest instructions from: https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart
- Implementation follows the official HTML/static site method described in the Vercel documentation

## Code Added
```html
<!-- Vercel Web Analytics -->
<script>
    window.va = window.va || function () { (window.vaq = window.vaq || []).push(arguments); };
</script>
<script defer src="https://cdn.vercel-insights.com/v1/script.js"></script>
```

## Notes
- No package manager installation was required for this static HTML project
- The analytics will automatically start tracking page views once deployed to Vercel
- The `defer` attribute ensures the script doesn't block page rendering
- The initialization script allows for potential future configuration via the `window.va()` API

## Testing
- ✅ HTML file validated and serves correctly (HTTP 200)
- ✅ Script tags properly inserted with correct syntax
- ✅ No existing functionality disrupted
- ✅ File structure and formatting preserved

## Next Steps
After deployment to Vercel:
1. The analytics will automatically begin collecting data
2. View analytics in the Vercel dashboard under your project's Analytics tab
3. Monitor the Network tab for requests to `/_vercel/insights/view` to confirm data collection
